{
  "name": "hzdb_run",
  "description": "Invoke any hzdb (Meta's Quest dev CLI) subcommand that isn't exposed as a dedicated MCP tool. hzdb is the standard CLI for Meta Quest VR/MR headset dev — like `gcloud` for GCP.\n\nPrefer a DEDICATED tool when one fits — they have richer schemas: hzdb_app (apps), hzdb_device (devices), hzdb_files (files), meta_docs_search / meta_docs_get_page (docs), get_device_logcat (logs), take_screenshot (screenshots).\n\nUse this catch-all for everything else: `perf` (capture / analyze / simpleperf), `ovrmetrics`, UI automation, audio control, casting, window mgmt, Unity editors, sideload, asset search, config, etc. The schema's `oneOf` enumerates every available subcommand with its real flags, defaults, and enum constraints — pick a subcommand path and pass typed args. For human-readable help on any subcommand tree, call hzdb_cli_help (topic=<group>).",
